" [:option {:value "964"} "10,000 metres, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "956"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "965"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "989"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "993"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "997"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "1001"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "1005"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "1013"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "1021"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "1029"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "1037"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "1046"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "1055"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "1064"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "1074"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "1084"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "1094"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "1108"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "1122"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "924500"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350644"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "9001025"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19020400"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15001100"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/530"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "500 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "13 February 1928 — 9:00"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/144"} "Olympia-Eisstadion Badrutts Park, St. Moritz"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/961"} "33 from 14 countries"]]] [:tr {:class "records", :style ""} [:th {:style "vertical-align: top;"} "Olympic Record "] [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/956"} "44.0"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/87537"} "Charley Jewtraw"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"] " / 26 January 1924 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/530"} "Details"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Starter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002493"} "Hermann Kleeberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002467"} "Henning Olsen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The red hot favorite for the gold in this discipline was Norwegian " [:a {:href "/athletes/89436"} "Roald Larsen"] ".  At the World Championships in Davos, which had been held little more than a week before this Olympic contest, he had bettered Oscar Mathisen’s 14-year-old World Record of 43.4 by three tenths of a second. This record had not brought him the World title, which was taken by " [:a {:href "/athletes/98260"} "Clas Thunberg"] ", a triple Olympic champion in Chamonix. The Finn Thunberg, bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/results/956"} "four years earlier"] ", was also a contender in the shortest event, as were the other Norwegians, " [:a {:href "/athletes/96283"} "Haakon Pedersen"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/96042"} "Oskar Olsen"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/85582"} "Bernt Evensen"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The North Americans were somewhat of an enigma to the Europeans. They had skated in Norway, but only against second-rate Norwegians or on imperial distances. The first pair of the 500 m, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/85627"} "John O’Neil Farrell"] " (USA) and Oskar Olsen (NOR), immediately showed what they were capable of. Farrell clocked 43.6, a new Olympic Record. The next race saw the two biggest title contenders pitted against each other. Roald Larsen took the early lead over Clas Thunberg, but the World Champion gained on the World Record holder in the back straight, making for an exciting sprint on the final 100 m. Thunberg won in an excellent time of 43.4, while Larsen equaled Farrell’s time. Haakon Pedersen went below 44 in the following race, but was already out of medal contention. The next big fight was between the two remaining Norwegians, Evensen and Olsen. The latter skated poorly, but 1927 World Champion Evensen went all out and stopped the watches at 43.4 - identical to Thunberg’s mark."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/85856"} "Jaakko Friman"] ", an outsider who had won the Finnish selection race for the Olympics, then also skated 43.6, making for two first place skaters, and three in third position. The last potential medalist was " [:a {:href "/athletes/86149"} "Charlie Gorman"] " of Canada. He skated against " [:a {:href "/athletes/88537"} "Wim Kos"] " (NED), who fell in the first curve. Gorman, who finished 7th in 43.9, claimed he was obstructed by his opponent’s fall. His protest was disallowed by the jury, which angered Gorman so much he withdrew from the " [:a {:href "/results/963"} "5,000 metres"] " held later that same day. The Dutchman did re-skate, albeit out of competition. Kos’ 47.5 would have ranked him an " [:em {} "ex aequo"] " 21st. He was also unlucky in his other Olympic races, falling in both the " [:a {:href "/results/962"} "1,500 m"] " and 5,000 m."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After the final pair, some of those in attendance expected tie-breaks for the title and third place, which was fairly common in those days. However, the rules did not allow for such a race and the result stood. It was the first time a gold medal was shared at the Winter Olympics. Evensen’s co-championship was the first speed skating gold for Norway."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button481932", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button481932').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "8"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/85582"} "Bernt Evensen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "43.4"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/98260"} "Clas Thunberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "43.4"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/85627"} "John O'Neil Farrell"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "43.6"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "12"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/85856"} "Jaakko Friman"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-cen